Blink checks the existing text of the focused editable as well, in its
ColdModeSpellCheckRequester, and Gecko checks the whole text of an
editor in mozInlineSpellChecker::EditorSpellCheckInited(), once
spellchecking starts for it. WebKit instead checks a whole text control
only when its spellcheck state changes, in HTMLTextFormControlElement::
effectiveSpellcheckAttributeChanged() — and otherwise checks each word
only as the caret leaves that word.
